# LeafyMind project rules

## Identity

AI concierge for Leafy Cave (Wellawaya, Sri Lanka). Guests plan via Agent Hub (`/hub`) or classic chat (`/chat`). Owners use `/owner`.

## Layer boundaries

| Layer | Path | Must not |
|-------|------|----------|
| Frontend | `frontend/src/` | Call LLM APIs; store secrets |
| BFF | `bff/` | Contain business logic; bypass backend auth |
| Backend | `backend/` | Expose stack traces to clients |
| DB | `db/migrations/` | Be edited without numbered SQL file |

## Documentation

When adding features, update:

- `README.md` (user-facing summary)
- `docs/API_REFERENCE.md` (new endpoints)
- `.env.example` (new env vars)
- `backend/config.py` (settings fields)

## Docker

- Food images: `frontend/public/images/food` → `/app/food_images`
- Public assets: `frontend/public` → `/app/public_assets`
- Ports from `.env`: `FRONTEND_PORT`, `BFF_PORT`, `BACKEND_PORT`

## Commits

Do not commit `.env`, `node_modules`, `__pycache__`, `.cache`, or secrets.
